# 🚨 MANDATORY TASK VERIFICATION WORKFLOW

## **CRITICAL: NEVER Mark Task Complete Without This Sequence**

### **Step 1: Reference Check (ALWAYS FIRST)**
```bash
# MANDATORY: Check auth-service patterns before ANY implementation
grep -r "require.*shared" backend/auth-service/
ls -la backend/auth-service/controllers/
cat backend/auth-service/controllers/authController.js | head -20
```

### **Step 2: Implementation Verification**
```bash
# Check ALL import paths in your service
grep -r "require.*shared" backend/service-name/

# Verify controller patterns match auth-service
grep -A 5 -B 5 "module.exports" backend/service-name/controllers/
```

### **Step 3: Docker Testing (MANDATORY)**
```bash
# 1. Restart Docker service
docker-compose restart service-name

# 2. Check logs for errors (CRITICAL)
docker logs logistics-service-name --tail=30

# 3. Look for MODULE_NOT_FOUND errors specifically
docker logs logistics-service-name | grep "MODULE_NOT_FOUND"

# 4. Test health endpoint
curl http://localhost:PORT/health | jq .

# 5. Test main API endpoints
curl -X GET http://localhost:PORT/api/endpoint
```

### **Step 4: Error Resolution (If Any Failures)**
```bash
# If MODULE_NOT_FOUND errors found:
# 1. Fix import paths to match auth-service
# 2. Restart Docker service again
# 3. Repeat verification until clean

# If service doesn't start:
# 1. Check Dockerfile and shared library setup
# 2. Verify middleware exports match auth-service
# 3. Test controller function exports
```

### **Step 5: Documentation Update (ONLY AFTER SUCCESS)**
```bash
# Update task status in BACKEND_TASK.md ONLY after:
# - Docker service starts successfully
# - Health endpoint responds
# - No MODULE_NOT_FOUND errors
# - API endpoints work
```

## **MANDATORY PATTERNS TO FOLLOW**

### **Import Paths (Check auth-service FIRST)**
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT (from controllers/routes/middleware/services)
const APIResponse = require("../shared/lib/response");
const logger = require("../shared/lib/logger");

// ✅ CORRECT (from server.js only)
const logger = require("./shared/lib/logger");

// ❌ FORBIDDEN (NEVER use these)
const APIResponse = require("../../shared/lib/response");
```

### **Controller Patterns (Match auth-service EXACTLY)**
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Function-based exports (like auth-service)
async function getEntity(req, res) {
  // Implementation
}

module.exports = {
  getEntity,
  createEntity,
  updateEntity
};

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Class-based exports
class EntityController {
  async getEntity(req, res) {}
}
module.exports = new EntityController();
```

### **Middleware Patterns (Check auth-service)**
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Check what auth-service exports
const { authenticate, authorize } = require("../middleware/auth");

// Use in routes exactly like auth-service does
router.get("/endpoint", authenticate, controller.method);
```

